body:
The editable Label <input> is always enabled, but handleUpdateLabel() no-ops in readOnly mode. This results in a controlled input that appears editable but cannot be changed. Consider setting the input to readOnly/disabled (or rendering plain text) when readOnly is true.
```suggestion
                    onChange={(e) => handleUpdateLabel(selectedComponent.id, e.target.value)}
                    readOnly={readOnly}
                    aria-readonly={readOnly}
```

The keydown handler deletes on Backspace/Delete but does not call preventDefault(). Backspace can trigger browser navigation when focus isn’t in an input, which would be a surprising/destructive behavior here. Call e.preventDefault() before deleting (like the other designers do).
```suggestion
        if (tag === 'INPUT' || tag === 'TEXTAREA') return;
        e.preventDefault();
```
